frog@gpu.utcs.utoronto.ca (F. Thinh-Ball) writes:
>For cryin' out loud! What colour was the corpse? Yellow!

It might be interesting to discuss how color can make nethack easier
to play.  However, most nethack players see corpses, and every other
game object, in black and white.  Some people see everything in life
in black and white, and most user interfaces tolerate that.

For people with color monitors, it is an interesting suggestion to
decide which objects to pick up based on their color.  This can save
some time given the current user interface.  However, the suggestion
seems very specific to the current version of nethack.  It is easy to
imagine future versions of nethack where some dangerous corpses are
not yellow, or where yellow food is quite common.

